   "entry": {
    "statement": "Theorem 1.2. For every fixed x in [1/\\sqrt2, 1] there exists \\sigma(x) in (0,\\infty), independent of D and of the inside approximation of Definition 1.1, such that h_\\delta/\\sigma(x) => \\Phi_D in D'(D). In particular the fields are tight as random distributions and, for every k >= 1 and f_1,...,f_k in C_c^\\infty(D), the vector (h_\\delta(f_i)/\\sigma(x))_{i<=k} converges to (\\Phi_D(f_i))_{i<=k}; all mixed moments of these vectors converge. Here h_\\delta is the integer Lipschitz height on the faces F_\\delta of \\delta H (hexagonal lattice) inside the cycle \\gamma_\\delta, zero on boundary faces, with P(h) proportional to x^{N_\\delta(h)}, N_\\delta(h) = number of adjacent face pairs with different heights; h_\\delta is extended as a constant on each face and paired with test functions by Euclidean area, h_\\delta(f)=\\int_D h_\\delta f dz; \\Phi_D is the zero-Dirichlet GFF with covariance G_D = (-\\Delta_D)^{-1}.",
