   "source": "S. Keel, K. Matsuki, J. McKernan, Log abundance theorem for threefolds, Duke Math. J. 75 (1994), no. 1, 99-119; read as the author-hosted PDF at https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~jmckerna/Papers/abu.pdf (24 pages, the URL in the bibliography entry), not the Duke typeset version.",
   "entry": {
    "statement": "(Log Abundance.) Let the pair $(X,\\Delta)$ consist of a threefold $X$ and boundary $\\Delta$, such that $K_X+\\Delta$ is nef and log canonical. Then $|m(K_X+\\Delta)|$ is basepoint free for some $m$.",
