   "entry": {
    "statement": "Let $f:X\\to Z$ be a surjective projective morphism of normal compact Kähler varieties with connected fibers, $(X,B+\\bbeta)$ a generalized pair which is gklt over an open subset $U$ of $Z$, such that $B+\\bbeta_X$ is modified big and $K_X+B+\\bbeta_X\\equiv f^*\\gamma$ for some $\\gamma\\in H^{1,1}_{\\rm BC}(Z)$. Then $(Z,\\DDelta_Z+\\ddelta)$ is a generalized pair such that $(U,\\DDelta|_U+\\ddelta)$ is gklt, i.e. (1) $\\DDelta_Z\\ge 0$; (2) $\\ddelta$ is b-nef (descends to some model $Z'$ with $\\ddelta_{Z'}$ nef); (3) the coefficients of components of $\\DDelta_{Z'}$ whose images meet $U$ are $<1$ for any birational model $Z'\\to Z$. Moreover, possibly after replacing $(X,B+\\bbeta)$ by a generalized pair $(X,B'+\\bbeta')$ with $K_X+B+\\bbeta_X\\equiv K_X+B'+\\bbeta'_X$ satisfying the same hypotheses, we may assume $\\ddelta_Z$ is modified big.",
