   "source": "OpenAI, A Conditional Reduction for Algebraic Kuga--Satake Correspondences (OpenAI Math Release preprint, September 10, 2026); read build/paper.tex and build/sections/introduction.tex of preprints/A-Conditional-Reduction-for-Algebraic-Kuga-Satake-Correspondences-September-10-2026 at commit adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a; Corollary 1.3 = \\label{main:all-degrees}.",
   "entry": {
    "statement": "If the hypothesis of Theorem 1.2 holds in the required polarized components in every degree, then (1.2) holds for every projective K3 surface. That is: assume that for every $d$ and every component of the moduli space of primitively amply polarized K3 surfaces of degree $2d$, condition (i) [an abelian variety $B$ and $\\alpha\\in CH^2(S\\times B)_{\\mathbb Q}$ with $\\alpha_*\\colon V\\to H^2(B,\\mathbb Q)$ nonzero, $V=h^\\perp$] or condition (ii) [a smooth connected projective surface $Y$ and a dominant generically finite $f\\colon Y\\to S$ with $f_*(\\mathrm{im}[\\wedge^2H^0(Y,\\Omega^1_Y)\\to H^0(Y,\\Omega^2_Y)])\\neq0$] of Theorem 1.1 holds very generally. Then every projective K3 surface $S$ admits $\\Gamma_S\\in CH^2(S\\times A_S\\times A_S)_{\\mathbb Q}$ with $(p_{AA})_*(\\mathrm{cl}(\\Gamma_S)\\cup p_S^*x)=\\kappa_S(x)$ for all $x\\in T(S)$, where $\\kappa_S\\colon T\\to W_S\\otimes W_S\\hookrightarrow H^2(A_S\\times A_S,\\mathbb Q)$ is the prescribed full Kuga-Satake map for all stipulated standard data on $T(S)$.",
