   "entry": {
    "statement": "Let $Y$ be a contact manifold with contact form $\\alpha$, $\\xi=\\ker\\alpha$, and symplectization $(\\mathbb R\\times Y, d(e^s\\alpha))$. Let $f_t\\colon\\Lambda\\to Y$, $t\\in[-1,1]$, be a self-transverse regular Legendrian homotopy, constant near its endpoints, connecting Legendrian embeddings $f_-$ and $f_+$, extended to all $t\\in\\mathbb R$ by $f_t=f_-$ for $t\\le -1$ and $f_t=f_+$ for $t\\ge 1$. Then there exists a self-transverse Lagrangian immersion $G\\colon \\mathbb R\\times\\Lambda\\to\\mathbb R\\times Y$, $G(t,x)=(h(x,t),\\tilde f_t(x))$, such that: (i) there is $T>0$ with $G(t,x)=(t,f_-(x))$ for $t<-T$ and $G(t,x)=(t,f_+(x))$ for $t>T$; (ii) $\\tilde f_t$ is $C^\\infty$-close to $f_t$; (iii) the double points of $G$ are in one-to-one index preserving correspondence with the double points of the regular homotopy $f_t$.",
