   "entry": {
    "statement": "Lemma 19.1 (Log-linear bound on rectangle crossing counts). There exists a constant c_lin in (0,1) (independent of c in [1,2]) such that for any n in Z_{>=0} and any rectangle R := [[w x \\rho w]] + u, with w >= 1, \\rho >= 1, u in R^2, \\mu_{Z^2}[ #AltHor^{\\bar\\omega}(R) >= 2n | E ] <= (1 - c_lin^{\\rho})^n, where E is any event measurable in terms of the even spins and edges at \\ell^\\infty-distance at least w/5 from R. Moreover the same bounds hold with \\mu_{Z^2} replaced by \\mu_{Cyl_L}, provided 2(\\rho+1/5)w <= L, with R regarded as a rectangle on the cylinder. Analogous bounds hold for vertical crossings, in the plane and on the cylinder. Here #AltHor^{\\bar\\omega}(R) is the maximal 2k such that \\bar\\omega=(\\omega^+,\\omega^-) has 2k alternating (\\omega^+,\\omega^-,...) left-right crossings of R.",
