   "entry": {
    "statement": "If $X$ is a compact normal Kähler variety, $\\alpha\\in H^{1,1}_{\\rm BC}(X)$ is big if $\\alpha\\ge\\omega$ where $\\omega$ is a Kähler current; equivalently, $\\alpha$ is big if it admits a Kähler current $T$ with $[T]\\in\\alpha$. If $f:X\\to Y$ is a birational morphism of normal varieties, then $f_*\\alpha$ is called modified big. Note: $f_*\\alpha$ may not be locally exact; however if $f_*\\alpha\\in H^{1,1}_{\\rm BC}(Y)$ and $Y$ is Kähler, then $f_*\\alpha$ is big.",
