   "entry": {
    "statement": "Let $X$ be a compact Fujiki class $\\mathcal C$ variety and $(X,B+\\bbeta)$ a generalized pair such that $B+\\bbeta_X$ is modified big. Then there is a generalized pair $(X,G+\\ggamma)$, a resolution $X'\\to X$ and a Kähler form $\\omega'$ on $X'$ such that $K_X+B+\\bbeta_X\\equiv K_X+G+\\ggamma_X$, $\\ggamma$ descends to $X'$, $\\ggamma_{X'}-\\omega'$ is nef, and ${\\rm NKLT}(X,B+\\bbeta)\\supset{\\rm NKLT}(X,G+\\ggamma)$, i.e. $\\mathcal J(X,B+\\bbeta)\\subset\\mathcal J(X,G+\\ggamma)$. In particular, setting $\\ddelta=\\ggamma-\\bar\\omega'$, $(X,G+\\ddelta)$ is a generalized pair. If $(X,B+\\bbeta)$ is gklt, then so is $(X,G+\\ggamma)$.",
