   "source": "C. Hacon, L. Xie, On the Kähler MMP and the transcendental base-point-free theorem, arXiv:2607.24986v1 [math.AG] (27 July 2026); LaTeX source KahlerBPF.tex of v1 read.",
   "entry": {
    "statement": "Let $f:X\\to Z$ be a Moishezon morphism and $X$ a Kähler variety with rational singularities. If there exists an $\\mathbb R$-line bundle $L$ such that $L\\equiv^{alg}_Z\\omega$ for a Kähler form $\\omega$ on $X$, that is $L\\cdot C=\\omega\\cdot C$ for all curves $C\\subset X$ with $f(C)=$ pt, then $f$ is strongly Moishezon. Moreover, if $X$ is smooth or strongly $\\mathbb Q$-factorial klt, then $f$ is projective.",
