   "entry": {
    "statement": "Proposition 2. Let -a < 0 < b. (1) When a+b < 2\\lambda, it is not possible to construct a BTLS A such that h_A \\in {-a, b} almost surely. (2) When a+b >= 2\\lambda, it is possible to construct a BTLS A_{-a,b} coupled with a GFF \\Gamma such that h_A \\in {-a,b} almost surely. Moreover the sets A_{-a,b} are: unique (if A' is another BTLS coupled with the same \\Gamma such that for all z in D, h_{A'}(z) \\in {-a,b} a.s., then A' = A_{-a,b} a.s.); measurable functions of the GFF \\Gamma they are coupled with; monotonic: if [a,b] \\subset [a',b'] and -a<0<b with a+b >= 2\\lambda, then a.s. A_{-a,b} \\subset A_{-a',b'}. Here \\lambda = \\sqrt{\\pi/8} and BTLS means bounded-type thin local set (local set with |h_A| <= K, isolated-component condition, and thinness (\\Gamma_A,f) = \\int_{D\\setminus A} h_A f).",
