   "entry": {
    "statement": "Lemma 7.3 (Cusp base change on the canonical branch; label lem:cusp-base-change). An ordinary section modulo $p^M$ on the canonical branch whose constant terms vanish, extended by zero on the other branches, is a section of $\\mathcal M_\\lambda/p^M$ over the ordinary open. The assertion remains true with coefficients in $\\mathcal O[t]/(p^M,t^b)$ and after finite extension of coefficients. Here $\\mathcal M_\\lambda=(Y^{tor}\\to X^{\\min})_*(\\mathcal E_\\lambda(-\\pi^*D))$, $\\pi:Y^{tor}\\to X^{tor}$ is the finite normalization in the generic-fiber level $J$, $D$ the reduced toroidal boundary of $X^{tor}$, and $\\mathcal E_\\lambda$ is built at each distinguished embedding from $(\\det\\omega^+)^{\\lambda_3}\\otimes\\mathcal D_d(\\omega^+)$, $\\mathcal D_d(\\mathcal H)=(\\mathrm{Sym}^d((\\wedge^2\\mathcal H)^\\vee))^\\vee$, $d=m-1$, and the opposite differential line to exponent $-\\lambda_4$; the canonical branch is the open and closed branch of Lemma 7.1 on which the rank-three flag equals the multiplicative subgroup.",
